if (vma->gpuva.flags & XE_VMA_PTE_2M)
return SZ_4K;
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the calculation for the maximum page size assumes that the VMA is always bound. If a VMA from an earlier operation is not yet bound, the code may incorrectly return a smaller page size (SZ_4K) instead of the maximum page size (SZ_1G), leading to potential skipping of REMAP operations.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
else if (vma->gpuva.flags & XE_VMA_PTE_4K)
return SZ_4K;
return SZ_1G;	/* Uninitialized, used max size */
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a check for the 4K page size flag and ensures that if the VMA is uninitialized (not bound), it defaults to returning the maximum page size (SZ_1G). This change ensures that the REMAP operations are handled correctly, preventing any skipping of operations due to incorrect page size assumptions.

